# RAG-Enhanced Search Technical Specification
# Version: 1.0.0
# Last Updated: 2025-02-05

@rag @search @hybrid
Feature: Hybrid Search System Technical Implementation
  As a development team
  We want to implement a hybrid RAG search system
  So that users can find relevant images through both semantic and graph-based queries

Background:
  Given the following system components are operational:
    | Component          | Status Check                                    | Implementation                    |
    | Vector Database   | Health check returns 200                        | src/lib/vector/vectorStore.js     |
    | Neo4j Graph DB    | Connection pool active                          | src/lib/neo4j/graphStore.js       |
    | Cache System      | Redis connection established                    | src/lib/cache/searchCache.js      |
  And test data is loaded:
    | Data Type         | Count | Characteristics                          |
    | Images           | 50  | Various styles, subjects, and attributes |
    | Users            | 5    | Mix of upload patterns                   |
    | Attributes       | 200   | Distributed across color, style, mood    |

@vector @implemented
Scenario: Semantic Vector Search Implementation
  Given the search index is initialized with current embeddings
    | Embedding Type    | Dimension | Model                |
    | Image            | 1536      | Claude 3.5         |
    | Text Query       | 1536      | Claude 3.5         |
  When executing a semantic search:
    ```javascript
    const results = await vectorSearch({
      query: "vibrant sunset with palm trees",
      limit: 20,
      minScore: 0.7
    })
    ```
  Then verify results structure:
    | Field            | Type    | Validation                              |
    | imageId         | string  | UUID format                             |
    | similarity      | float   | Range 0.0-1.0                           |
    | attributes      | array   | Non-empty                               |
    | matchingTerms   | array   | Contains query terms                    |
  And performance metrics meet:
    | Metric           | Threshold | Measurement Method                     |
    | Latency         | < 200ms   | Response time without cache           |
    | Precision@10    | > 0.7     | Manual relevance assessment          |
    | Recall@20       | > 0.8     | Known relevant items retrieved       |

@graph @implemented
Scenario: Graph Pattern Search Implementation
  Given the Neo4j database contains valid relationships:
    ```cypher
    MATCH (i:Image)-[r:HAS_ATTRIBUTE]->(a:Attribute)
    WHERE r.prominence > 0.5
    RETURN count(distinct i) as images, count(r) as relationships
    ```
  When executing a graph search:
    ```javascript
    const results = await graphSearch({
      patterns: [{
        type: 'HAS_ATTRIBUTE',
        value: 'crimson',
        minProminence: 0.8
      }],
      limit: 20
    })
    ```
  Then verify graph traversal:
    | Aspect           | Requirement                                   |
    | Path Depth      | Maximum 3 hops                               |
    | Relationship    | Valid HAS_ATTRIBUTE connections              |
    | Properties      | All required metadata present                |
  And results include:
    | Property         | Validation Rule                              |
    | pathScore       | Calculated based on relationship weights     |
    | nodeProperties  | Complete attribute metadata                  |
    | relationships   | Array of traversed edges                     |

@hybrid @implemented
Scenario: Hybrid Result Ranking Implementation
  Given both vector and graph searches return results
  When merging results using hybrid algorithm:
    ```javascript
    const hybridResults = await hybridSearch({
      query: "sunset photos with red colors",
      weights: {
        vector: 0.6,
        graph: 0.3,
        recency: 0.1
      }
    })
    ```
  Then verify ranking logic:
    | Factor           | Weight | Calculation Method                       |
    | Vector Score    | 60%    | Cosine similarity                       |
    | Graph Score     | 30%    | Path relevance * prominence             |
    | Recency        | 10%    | Normalized timestamp difference         |
  And results are sorted by:
    ```javascript
    finalScore = (
      vectorScore * 0.6 +
      graphScore * 0.3 +
      recencyScore * 0.1
    )
    ```

@cache @implemented
Scenario: Search Result Caching Implementation
  Given the cache system is initialized:
    ```javascript
    const cache = new SearchCache({
      ttl: 300, // 5 minutes
      maxSize: '1GB'
    })
    ```
  When caching search results:
    | Operation        | Implementation                                |
    | Cache Key       | SHA256(query + params)                       |
    | Value Format    | Compressed JSON of results                   |
    | Invalidation    | On image updates affecting results           |
  Then verify cache behavior:
    | Aspect           | Requirement                                   |
    | Hit Rate        | > 80% for repeated queries                   |
    | Latency         | < 50ms on cache hit                         |
    | Consistency     | Match fresh results 100%                     |

@error @implemented
Scenario Outline: Error Handling Implementation
  Given potential error conditions:
    | Error Type       | HTTP Code | Response Format                         |
    | Invalid Query   | 400       | {error: string, details: object}       |
    | Auth Failed     | 401       | {error: string}                        |
    | Timeout        | 503       | {error: string, retryAfter: number}   |
  When error occurs in <component>
  Then system should respond with <status> and <message>

  Examples:
    | Component        | Status | Message                                   |
    | Vector Search   | 400    | "Invalid vector dimensions"              |
    | Graph Search    | 503    | "Graph database unavailable"             |
    | Cache           | 500    | "Cache system error"                     |

